target=\"_blank\"` to open a link in a new tab without an icon. `isExternal` adds an icon and defaults\nto `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`; explicit `target` and `rel` override those defaults.\nYou can also compose an `Icon` as a child independently of navigation behavior."},"169":{"id":"/docs/components/button-20","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use the `CloseButton` preset to dismiss an overlay (such as a `Modal`). It defaults to `slot=\"close\"`, so it picks up the overlay's close behavior with no wiring, and always renders an `x` icon with `aria-label=\"Close\"`. For a labelled dismiss action (e.g. \"Cancel\"), use a raw `<Button slot=\"close\">Cancel</Button>`."},"170":{"id":"/docs/components/button-21","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Inside a field `Group`, `slot=\"control\"` and `slot=\"trigger\"` pick up the matching look, size, and\ndisabled state from context. See TextField for control affixes, and Select or DatePicker for trigger faces.\nThe `control` and `trigger` variants are field parts: the field sizes them, so use them only inside a field."},"171":{"id":"/docs/components/button-22","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#default","content":"The default/tertiary button is the base for all other buttons in the system. It provides no significant visual treatment other than to provide indication for the user to take a common action."},"172":{"id":"/docs/components/button-23","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."},"173":{"id":"/docs/components/button-24","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."},"174":{"id":"/docs/components/button-25","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."},"175":{"id":"/docs/components/button-26","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"The critical button signifies to the user a destructive action will take place."},"176":{"id":"/docs/components/button-27","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Any button variant can be disabled to prevent interaction, communicated with reduced opacity and a not-allowed cursor."},"177":{"id":"/docs/components/button-28","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"You may provide an optional `Icon` component to the button. Wrap the text beside an icon in a `Text`. If you do not include text, you must provide an aria-label attribute to identify the purpose of the button. This will produce a square button."},"178":{"id":"/docs/components/button-29","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icons-and-alignment","content":"Control navigation with `target` and `rel`, and compose icons independently. Stretched inline content follows the browser's default alignment; other variants stay centered."},"179":{"id":"/docs/components/button-30","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#inline","content":"The inline button sits within a run of text, styled like a link while retaining button semantics."},"180":{"id":"/docs/components/button-31","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#minimal","content":"The minimal button is an icon-only button that's used when space is limited and/or when the action is universally understood."},"181":{"id":"/docs/components/button-32","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#sizes","content":"Buttons come in small, medium, and large sizes to fit different layout densities. Without\n`size`, a button follows the surrounding size scope, and uses medium outside any scope. An\nicon-only button is square and as tall as a text button of the same size."},"182":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"page","content":"Calendar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar"},"183":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar","content":"Accessible calendar grids for selecting a single date (Calendar) or a date range (RangeCalendar), built on React Aria."},"184":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Features"},"185":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#installation","content":"Installation"},"186":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#working-with-dates","content":"Working with dates"},"187":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#examples","content":"Examples"},"188":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#default","content":"Default"},"189":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#with-value","content":"With value"},"190":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#range","content":"Range"},"191":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#min--max","content":"Min / Max"},"192":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#unavailable","content":"Unavailable"},"193":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"194":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"195":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"196":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"197":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#props","content":"Props"},"198":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#calendar","content":"Calendar"},"199":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#rangecalendar","content":"RangeCalendar"},"200":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-17","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Single-date (`Calendar`) and range (`RangeCalendar`) grids built on React Aria"},"201":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-18","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Month dropdown plus a typeable year input in the header for fast navigation"},"202":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-19","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Keyboard navigable and screen-reader announced"},"203":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-20","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"},"204":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-21","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Date-only values via `@internationalized/date`'s `CalendarDate`"},"205":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-22","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#working-with-dates","content":"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"},"206":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-23","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#working-with-dates","content":"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."},"207":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-24","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#default","content":"A single-date calendar."},"208":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-25","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#with-value","content":"A calendar with a pre-selected date."},"209":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-26","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#range","content":"Selecting a start and end date."},"210":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-27","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#min--max","content":"Bounding selectable dates."},"211":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-28","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#unavailable","content":"Disabling scattered individual dates with `isDateUnavailable`."},"212":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-29","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#disabled","content":"A fully disabled calendar."},"213":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-30","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Arrow keys move by day; PageUp/PageDown by month; Home/End to row edges"},"214":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-31","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Focus-visible outline; disabled days are not focusable"},"215":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-32","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Out-of-month days render at reduced opacity and are not selectable"},"216":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-33","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Always provide an `aria-label` on standalone calendars."},"217":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-34","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Use `isDateUnavailable` for scattered disabled days; use `minValue` / `maxValue` for contiguous bounds."},"218":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-35","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#troubleshooting","content":"Dates not formatting per locale? Ensure the app is wrapped in `<I18nProvider locale=\"…\">`."},"219":{"id":"/docs/components/card","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"page","content":"Card","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card"},"220":{"id":"/docs/components/card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"A surface that groups related content and actions."},"221":{"id":"/docs/components/card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#installation","content":"Installation"},"222":{"id":"/docs/components/card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#examples","content":"Examples"},"223":{"id":"/docs/components/card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#default","content":"Default"},"224":{"id":"/docs/components/card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#text-lockup","content":"Text lockup"},"225":{"id":"/docs/components/card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#corner-actions","content":"Corner actions"},"226":{"id":"/docs/components/card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#link","content":"Link"},"227":{"id":"/docs/components/card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#grouped-links","content":"Grouped links"},"228":{"id":"/docs/components/card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#media","content":"Media"},"229":{"id":"/docs/components/card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#actions","content":"Actions"},"230":{"id":"/docs/components/card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#multiple-selection","content":"Multiple selection"},"231":{"id":"/docs/components/card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#single-selection","content":"Single selection"},"232":{"id":"/docs/components/card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"233":{"id":"/docs/components/card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#layout","content":"Layout"},"234":{"id":"/docs/components/card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"Customization"},"235":{"id":"/docs/components/card-15","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"236":{"id":"/docs/components/card-16","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#props","content":"Props"},"237":{"id":"/docs/components/card-17","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#card","content":"Card"},"238":{"id":"/docs/components/card-18","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#cardgroup","content":"CardGroup"},"239":{"id":"/docs/components/card-19","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#cardselectionindicator","content":"CardSelectionIndicator"},"240":{"id":"/docs/components/card-20","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"Card groups related content, like media, text, and actions, on a single surface. On its own, a Card\nis a static surface, or a link when you pass `href`. Put Cards in a `CardGroup` to make them\nselectable or to give them an action: the group owns selection, row actions, focus, and arrow-key\nnavigation."},"241":{"id":"/docs/components/card-21","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#default","content":"A static Card just renders its children."},"242":{"id":"/docs/components/card-22","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#text-lockup","content":"Compose Card with TextLockup for eyebrow, title, and body."},"243":{"id":"/docs/components/card-23","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#corner-actions","content":"Direct CornerActions sit at the top-end of the Card."},"244":{"id":"/docs/components/card-24","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#link","content":"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, so layered content like an elevated Box stays\nclickable. The link takes its name from its content unless you pass `aria-label`. Do not nest\ncontrols in a link Card."},"245":{"id":"/docs/components/card-25","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#grouped-links","content":"Linked Cards in a CardGroup navigate on a press or Enter. Arrow keys move between rows, and\nnested controls keep their own actions. Disable a Card to prevent its navigation."},"246":{"id":"/docs/components/card-26","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#media","content":"Use default padding for inset media, or zero Card padding with a padded lockup for full bleed.\nMedia can stand alone, follow the text, or be a custom Box. Clip only the media region."},"247":{"id":"/docs/components/card-27","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#actions","content":"Inside a CardGroup, `onAction` runs when the row is pressed or activated with Enter. Nested\nbuttons keep their own presses, so Save does not open the Modal. Compose a Card inside the Modal\nwhen the action is a focused form."},"248":{"id":"/docs/components/card-28","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#multiple-selection","content":"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` lets each Card toggle on its own. CardSelectionIndicator shows the\nstate, and its children can render custom content from it. Nested buttons keep their own presses."},"249":{"id":"/docs/components/card-29","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#single-selection","content":"`selectionMode=\"single\"` keeps one Card selected at a time. Arrow keys move between Cards, and\nSpace selects the focused one."},"250":{"id":"/docs/components/card-30","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#disabled","content":"`isDisabled` fades the Card. A disabled link Card does not navigate, and a disabled Card in a\nCardGroup cannot be selected, run its action, or take focus. `disabledKeys` on the group does\nthe same by key."},"251":{"id":"/docs/components/card-31","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#layout","content":"Use Grid for responsiveness."},"252":{"id":"/docs/components/card-32","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"`CardSelectionIndicator` only shows a Card's selection state. The `CardGroup` owns selection, so a\nCard stays selectable without an indicator. Pass non-interactive children or a selection-state\nrender function to replace the default circle and icon. See the Multiple selection example."},"253":{"id":"/docs/components/card-33","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"Card link options such as `target`, `rel`, `download`, and `routerOptions` apply to both standalone\nlinks and linked rows in a `CardGroup`. A `CardGroup` ref points to its collection surface. Card ids\naccept strings or numbers; numeric keys keep their type in group selection and become strings on\nstandalone DOM elements."},"254":{"id":"/docs/components/card-34","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"To style a Card by state, target `[data-selected]`, `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`,\n`[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` from your `className`."},"255":{"id":"/docs/components/card-35","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"A `CardGroup` is a grid: each Card is a row, Tab moves into and out of the group, and arrow keys\nmove between Cards. Name the group with `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Each Card takes its\naccessible name from `textValue`, which also drives typeahead. Plain-text children supply it by\ndefault, so set `textValue` when a Card's content is composed."},"256":{"id":"/docs/components/card-36","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"In a selectable group, Space toggles the focused Card. Without selection, `onAction` runs on Enter\nor a press. Do not combine them: with both, a press runs the action and only Space selects, so\npointer users cannot select."},"257":{"id":"/docs/components/card-37","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Use Antares controls such as `Button`, `LinkButton`, and `Checkbox` inside a grouped Card. React\nAria keeps their presses independent of row selection and actions. For a custom press target,\nuse `Pressable` and forward its props and ref to the target."},"258":{"id":"/docs/components/card-38","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Set `keyboardNavigationBehavior=\"tab\"` on `CardGroup` to move through controls within a row with\nTab. Native controls follow React Aria's event propagation rules."},"259":{"id":"/docs/components/card-39","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"A `CardGroup` does not submit form values. Read the selection from `onSelectionChange`."},"260":{"id":"/docs/components/card-40","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"`href` on a standalone Card renders the Card itself as a native link, named by its content unless\nyou pass `aria-label`. A link Card cannot contain controls, so do not put CornerActions, buttons,\nor inputs in it. Inside a `CardGroup`, `href` navigates from the row instead."},"261":{"id":"/docs/components/card-41","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"`isDisabled` fades the Card. On a link Card it stops navigation. In a `CardGroup` it also stops\nselection, the action, and focus, as does listing the Card's `id` in `disabledKeys`."},"262":{"id":"/docs/components/card-42","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"On a static Card, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, and `aria-describedby` apply to the surface,\nfor example with `role=\"region\"`."},"263":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"page","content":"Carousel","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel"},"264":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-0","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel","content":"The Carousel component allows users to cycle through a series of content panels (typically images, cards, or text) in a horizontal or vertical layout. It is commonly used for featured content, product showcases, or testimonials."},"265":{"id"