g DOM size and improving performance when the same icon appears multiple times"],[1022,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1379,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1667,"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"],[1020,"**Value scale**: `minValue`, `maxValue`, `step`, and `formatOptions` configure the numeric behavior"],[1931,"**Verify event targets**: Tooltips use mouse event coordinates and bar group positions"],[1868,"**Vertical and horizontal orientations**: Choose the best layout for your data and use case"],[1907,"**Vertical charts**: Horizontal scrolling when many data points exceed container width"],[1877,"**VisX integration**: Leverages VisX primitives for scales, axes, shapes, and responsive layout"],[767,"**What happens with sprite mode:**"],[1497,"`--color-input-background-default`"],[1494,"`--color-input-background-selected`"],[1503,"`--color-input-text-default`"],[1504,"`--ux-1glcx6s`"],[1492,"`--ux-1m9ys0v`"],[1498,"`--ux-1nu8itt`"],[1501,"`--ux-1sbfig8`"],[1495,"`--ux-sywk25`"],[1507,"`--ux-zvaw3s`"],[206,"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."],[2132,"`<Box blockAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2134,"`<Box inlineAlignChildren=\"center\">`"],[2128,"`<Box orientation=\"horizontal\">`"],[2130,"`<Box orientation=\"vertical\">`"],[2135,"`<Flex alignItems=\"center\">`"],[2131,"`<Flex direction=\"column\" >`"],[2129,"`<Flex direction=\"row\" >`"],[2133,"`<Flex justifyContent=\"center\">`"],[2085,"`2xl` - 2x extra large spacing"],[605,"`acceptedFileTypes` is a best-effort filter for the OS picker — always validate file type and size again in your `onSelect` handler, since it can be bypassed."],[1704,"`align` centers the parts as well as the text, so a `Tag` eyebrow stays centered too."],[1223,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[1348,"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"],[450,"`aria-describedby` wires the `helperText` to the progressbar for screen readers"],[343,"`aria-disabled` for disabled checkboxes"],[1224,"`aria-disabled` for disabled options"],[1349,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[345,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1226,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1783,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1350,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[449,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1124,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[344,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1225,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[447,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1122,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1121,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[446,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1123,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[448,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2077,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[495,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[205,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[252,"`CardSelectionIndicator` only shows a Card's selection state. The `CardGroup` owns selection, so a\nCard stays selectable without an indicator. Pass non-interactive children or a selection-state\nrender function to replace the default circle and icon. See the Multiple selection example."],[1888,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[329,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[399,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[417,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[395,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[410,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1825,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[486,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[496,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[497,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[488,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[2045,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1158,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[742,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[745,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[741,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[743,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[744,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[746,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1485,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[535,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1635,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[569,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[653,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1626,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1634,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1068,"`Enter/Space`"],[92,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[493,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[632,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[836,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[578,"`Escape`"],[964,"`Escape`"],[1070,"`Escape`"],[1830,"`Escape`"],[604,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2114,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[750,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2152,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[655,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[260,"`href` on a standalone Card renders the Card itself as a native link, named by its content unless\nyou pass `aria-label`. A link Card cannot contain controls, so do not put CornerActions, buttons,\nor inputs in it. Inside a `CardGroup`, `href` navigates from the row instead."],[244,"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, so layered content like an elevated Box stays\nclickable. The link takes its name from its content unless you pass `aria-label`. Do not nest\ncontrols in a link Card."],[500,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[824,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[853,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[250,"`isDisabled` fades the Card. A disabled link Card does not navigate, and a disabled Card in a\nCardGroup cannot be selected, run its action, or take focus. `disabledKeys` on the group does\nthe same by key."],[261,"`isDisabled` fades the Card. On a link Card it stops navigation. In a `CardGroup` it also stops\nselection, the action, and focus, as does listing the Card's `id` in `disabledKeys`."],[2028,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[656,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2083,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[883,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2082,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[918,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[203,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[538,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[957,"`Modal` accepts `isOpen` and `onOpenChange` directly, so it can be controlled without a\n`ModalTrigger`. Useful when the modal is opened from several places at once."],[952,"`ModalTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Modal>`, handling open state automatically. Based on RAC `DialogTrigger`."],[1157,"`orientation` switches between `horizontal` (accent bar on top) and `vertical` (accent bar on the leading edge)."],[1880,"`orientation=\"horizontal\"` swaps the axes: categories run 